Here are my "it would be cool if someone else did them" business ideas
of the moment:

1. An employment agency for people who want to telecommute.It seems as
though there are a lot more people who want to telecommute than there
are bosses who are willing to accept telecommuters--there should be
a niche for someone who can find that minority of employers. I've
heard one person say that he'd literally take half his present salary
if he could telecommute.....

2. A shoe company to be called Foot-Shaped Shoes. If you look at your
foot and look at a shoe, you will discover that they are not the same
shape. This is ridiculous. People's feet are fairly blunt on the toe
end, and shoes should be the same shape.

The big research project at Foot-Shaped Shoes would be an effort to
invent a satisfactory-looking flat woman's dress shoe. My tentative
theory is that it would be some sort of ornamented sandal.

3. A national magazine for bouncers--this sounds like a profession
with certain amount of detail and a tendency to produce interesting
stories.

4. A national magazine for people with mediocre jobs--it would 
include best regions, best and worst companies to work for, how
to upgrade skills, job-finding methods, and revenge fantasies.

5. A hospital based on what is known about what makes people feel
better--it would be pleasant-looking, offer good food and uninterrupted
sleep, and probably assign each patient an ombudsman.

Foot-Shaped Shoes is the only one of these products that I see an
immediate personal use for, though.

